hi friends this is probably the most  exciting day of my life next to the  birth of my child  and my wedding day former wwe star gabby  tuff  came out as transgender on thursday via  instagram  and got candid about her journey i am  amazed at the overwhelming show of  support the 42 year old shared  this pic on instagram posing in front of  a framed photo of herself when she was  still known by her ring name  tyler rex gabby penned a lengthy caption  which read in part quote  unashamed unabashedly me this is the  side of me that has hidden in the  shadows  afraid and fearful of what the world  would think afraid of what my family  friends and followers would say  or do i am no longer afraid and i am no  longer fearful  i can now say with confidence that i  love myself  for who i am gabby who retired from the  wwe in 2014  noted that the past eight months have  been the darkest of her entire life  the emotional turmoil of being  transgender and having to face the world  has almost ended me on multiple  occasions  however the day i stopped caring about  what other people thought  was the day i truly became limitless and  allowed my authentic self  to come into the light i haven't even  begun to read  the messages i've just seen some of the  banners coming in and  i am blown away the athlete has been  married to her wife priscilla  since 2002 and they share a  nine-year-old daughter mia  gaby thanked her friends and family for  accepting her for who she is  adding i don't expect everyone to agree  or understand  it's not my place to change any of your  core beliefs  just know the outer shell may change but  the soul remains the same  i just want to say thank you to everyone  that held support for me  before the world knew you know who you  are on wednesday prior to coming out as  transgender gabby shared a tribute to  priscilla  calling her her twin flame quote we  stand by each other's side  fully supporting without judgment  without opinion bonded by lifetimes of  pain  heartache joy happiness passion  irreplaceable experiences  births and deaths and we are both free  and more in love than  any lifetime before on thursday gabby  thanked her fans for their love  and support on her insta story thank you  for everyone with the flood of  positive messages coming in i love you  all so much  and on friday she shared a montage of  clips  including this moment with priscilla  dancing  in the bathroom
 

